[00:09.11]A: I used to rule the world
[00:12.80]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:15.28]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:19.60]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:36.59]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:40.65]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:43.91]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:47.72]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:50.56]A: One minute I held the key
[00:54.53]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:57.20]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:01.46]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:05.28]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:09.16]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:12.62]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:15.74]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:19.54]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:22.94]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:25.57]A: Never an honest word
[01:29.28]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:45.93]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:50.10]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:52.79]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:57.15]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[02:00.34]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:04.18]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:06.63]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:11.20]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:14.97]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:18.57]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:21.98]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:25.44]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:28.92]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:32.50]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:35.69]A: Never an honest word
[02:38.76]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:11.10]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:14.15]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:17.73]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:21.01]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:24.63]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:28.09]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[03:31.23]A: Never an honest word
[03:34.47]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
